   |
Firewall
   |
Internet/Azure

---

# Azure Equivalent

Traditional VLAN:
Physical segmentation

Azure Equivalent:
- VNet
- Subnet
- NSG
- Route Table

Azure uses software-defined segmentation instead of physical VLANs.

---

# Interview Explanation

“VNet peering allows secure private communication between VNets using Microsoft backbone infrastructure. Azure internally routes traffic using Software Defined Networking. VLANs provide logical Layer 2 segmentation using VLAN tags, while Layer 3 devices perform routing between VLANs. Data flows from Application Layer down to Physical Layer through encapsulation and travels across the network.”

